    "title": "Public Holidays - PublicHolidays.bz",
    "text": "Today – 15 April 2026 – is not a holiday in Belize.Discover upcoming public holiday dates for Belize and start planning to make the most of your time off. Skip down to:2026 Public Holidays2027 Public Holidays2028 Public Holidays 2026 Public Holidays DateDayHoliday1 JanThuNew Year's Day 15 JanThuGeorge Price Day 9 MarMonNational Heroes and Benefactors Day 3 AprFriGood Friday 4 AprSatHoly Saturday 6 AprMonEaster Monday 1 MayFriLabour Day 1 AugSatEmancipation Day 10 SepThuSaint George's Caye Day 21 SepMonIndependence Day 12 OctMonIndigenous Peoples' Resistance Day 19 NovThuGarifuna Settlement Day 25 DecFriChristmas Day 26 DecSatBoxing Day Visit pressoffice.gov.bz for the original release. 2027 Public Holidays DateDayHoliday1 JanFriNew Year's Day 15 JanFriGeorge Price Day 8 MarMonNational Heroes and Benefactors Day 26 MarFriGood Friday 27 MarSatHoly Saturday 28 MarSunEaster Sunday 29 MarMonEaster Monday 1 MaySatLabour Day 1 AugSunEmancipation Day 2 AugMonEmancipation Day Holiday 10 SepFriSaint George's Caye Day 21 SepTueIndependence Day 11 OctMonIndigenous Peoples' Resistance Day 19 NovFriGarifuna Settlement Day 25 DecSatChristmas Day 26 DecSunBoxing Day 27 DecMonBoxing Day Holiday The dates in this table are an estimate. We will update this page once the official public holiday dates for 2027 are released. 2028 Public Holidays DateDayHoliday1 JanSatNew Year's Day 15 JanSatGeorge Price Day 6 MarMonNational Heroes and Benefactors Day 14 AprFriGood Friday 15 AprSatHoly Saturday 17 AprMonEaster Monday 1 MayMonLabour Day 1 AugTueEmancipation Day 10 SepSunSaint George's Caye Day 11 SepMonSaint George's Caye Holiday 21 SepThuIndependence Day 9 OctMonIndigenous Peoples' Resistance Day 19 NovSunGarifuna Settlement Day 20 NovMonGarifuna Settlement Holiday 25 DecMonChristmas Day 26 DecTueBoxing Day The dates in this table are an estimate. We will update this page once the official public holiday dates for 2028 are released. Belize celebrates 11 national holidays each year, with the Easter holiday taking place over a four-day celebration. A few of the country’s holidays are religious based and the dates change each year based on the lunar cycle. Public holidays are governed by the Chapter 289 of the Laws of Belize, Holiday Acts. These acts establish which days are official holidays in Belize. The government reserves the right to add days, remove days, and to change mid-week holidays or those falling on a Sunday to another day so that all can benefit from observing the holiday. The Labour Code, Part XI, Section 117 states that all employees must receive a paid day off for nationally recognised holidays and that employers who pay by the piece or by the job performed must provide an “average day’s pay” for their employees. If an employee is obligated to work on a holiday due to the nature of their job, the law requires that employees receive additional pay for their duties. On Christmas, Good Friday and Easter Monday, employees must be paid at double their hourly or daily rate. On all other holidays, employees receive their regular pay plus one half more for these dates.",
